// The Root Chapel (Chapel_2): Teodor teaches Inkthread, the Unwriters' solvent-line reversed (bible 4.3).
// And the Lantern Grove vigil (Grove_2): eleven lanterns, eleven villages, in the present tense. No choices (8.3).

title: RootChapel_Teodor_Thread
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.teodor.thread")>>
    Teodor: The line holds. Draw it the way you would draw a road you mean to walk back along. #still #line:097d75f
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if not has_flag("verdance.teodor.met")>>
    Teodor: The chapel is for the brothers, cartographer. Come up to the cloister first. I will find you. #still #line:0798149
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: The Cantors draw a line to let go. A thread of solvent, from the place to nothing. #line:029e48a
Teodor: Draw it the other way. It is the same line. #plant:5.6 #line:0a3ac8c
-> From the place to me. #line:05fa354
    <<voice surveyor verdance>>
    Teodor: Yes. From the place to you. Then it holds your weight, because you are holding it. #face:bright #line:090fbc1
-> That's a Guild tether. #line:001e4ff
    <<voice warden verdance>>
    Teodor: A tether goes into the white. This goes across it. The Guild never learned the difference. #face:wary #line:0d11e67
-> ... #line:07ea8e1
    <<voice drift verdance>>
    Teodor: Watch the root, not your hand. There. Again. #line:0f42bad
Teodor: The birds who built this chapel crossed to the grove without a thread. We need one. It is enough. #face:grave #line:0cc6ef9
<<grant Inkthread>>
<<flag verdance.teodor.thread 1>>
===

title: Grove_Teodor_Vigil
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.grove.vigil")>>
    Teodor: Eleven. They are all here tonight. #still #face:grave #line:07d0886
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Teodor: Sit. There is nothing to say. I will say it anyway. #face:grave #line:0c00c21
Teodor: Wenlow has a well with a crooked bucket. Nobody fixes it. They like the sound. #face:bright #line:0fe40ab
Teodor: Harrowby bakes on the seventh day. The whole lane smells of it. #face:bright #line:0bdbd62
Teodor: Coldmere is cold. It says so on the sign. #face:bright #line:06b2728
Teodor: Ashcross has two churches and one bell between them. They argue about it every Sunday. #face:bright #line:0763519
Teodor: Nettlecombe keeps bees. The bees are not anchored. They leave every spring and come back. #face:bright #line:01af9f9
Teodor: Brindle is small. Brindle is very small. #face:bright #line:068f721
Teodor: Fenn has a ferry that crosses a river that is not there any more. The ferryman is patient. #face:grave #line:004d129
Teodor: Scarsby has a school. The same eleven children are in it. #face:grave #line:0138570
Teodor: Tollan is on a hill. You can see Halden from it on a clear day. #face:bright #line:0bbb398
Teodor: Ettle is where my mother lives. She is seventy. She is always seventy. #face:grave #line:0f7637e
Teodor: Marrowgate is the last. Marrowgate is waiting for me to be sure. #face:grave #line:004d011
Teodor: That is all of them. Thank you for sitting. #face:grave #line:09f9733
Teodor: Carry the eleven, if you would. In that order. Somebody besides me should have them right. #face:grave #line:0ad3676
<<bind teodor.eleven_names>>
<<flag verdance.grove.vigil 1>>
===
